B.a2x=new A.aR("Each chart is its own org. Search by name or website, star favorites, and tap New org chart under the list.\n\nCharts for your signed-in account load on Home. Backup and sync is in the \xb7\xb7\xb7 menu and starts off \u2014 turn it on to keep every chart file in that Google Drive or OneDrive folder. Share a chart from inside it \u2014 not from home. You can send a PDF, or an Orgora file the other person opens in the app.\n\nInside a chart: tap a person to edit them, drag to change who reports to whom, and use the view-mode control to switch between compact titles and full detail.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5c=new A.fS(B.iL,"Charts",B.a2x,null)
B.LI=new A.bK(62072,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.a1I=new A.aR("Add someone from the chart, import contacts from a connected mailbox, or import a LinkedIn profile (More \u2192 Import from LinkedIn).\n\nFind people in your inbox (home screen) scans your own mail for work addresses and suggests a chart per domain. Personal mail domains are grouped separately and are never suggested as a company chart.\n\nInbox imports land in a list on the left, not on the tree. Drag someone onto a person to make them a report, or onto empty canvas for a top-level seat. Anyone you leave in the list stays off the hierarchy.\n\nLong-press a card to drag that person under a new manager.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5d=new A.fS(B.LI,"People",B.a1I,null)
B.Lz=new A.bK(61284,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.a2e=new A.aR("After you sign in with Google Drive or Microsoft OneDrive, Backup and sync is in the home \xb7\xb7\xb7 menu. The switch starts off, so nothing uploads until you turn it on. Each chart is one Orgora file in that account. The file is not Pro and not a public link. There is no Orgora server.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5e=new A.fS(B.Lz,"Save a chart",B.a2e,null)
B.Lr=new A.bK(58289,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.a26=new A.aR("Your Google or Microsoft sign-in is your Orgora identity. Chart files live in your own Drive or OneDrive (and may cache on this device). Orgora never hosts the file and does not offer it as a public link. No separate Orgora account database, no analytics, and no tracking. Optional inbox connect and LinkedIn clipping talk only to your provider or stay on-device. Sign out from Home \xb7\xb7\xb7 clears the SSO session on this device.\n\nPrivacy policy: https://sdkaihub.com/orgora-charts/privacy.html",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5f=new A.fS(B.Lr,"Privacy",B.a26,null)
B.a21=new A.aR("Orgora Clipper copies a LinkedIn profile into the app. Nothing is sent to us. After you clip, a banner lists people waiting, or open More \u2192 Import from LinkedIn.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.Hk=new A.PN(null)
B.Ok=s([B.a21,B.aN,B.Hk],t.p)
B.IM=new A.CA(B.a9,B.p,B.H,B.ao,null,B.cv,null,0,B.Ok,null)
B.a5g=new A.fS(B.qT,"Import from LinkedIn",B.IM,null)
B.a1U=new A.aR("Grok, Claude, and GPT are labeled Beta. Beta does not mean the marketplace listing is approved. None of those listings are approved.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5h=new A.fS(B.qU,"Connectors",B.a1U,null)
B.Lq=new A.bK(58189,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.a1S=new A.aR("Open a chart, then Share (not the home \xb7\xb7\xb7 menu). Send a PDF picture, or an Orgora file the other person opens in Orgora Charts.\n\nViewing a shared chart is free. Creating a new chart from one still follows the free-tier size limits unless you are Pro.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5i=new A.fS(B.Lq,"Sharing a chart",B.a1S,null)
B.a1Y=new A.aR("Create products (the software you sell) and use cases (the pains and outcomes that matter). Tag them onto people.\n\nWhen a use case is linked to a product, the person card shows them on one row: product on the left, use case on the right. Unlinked tags get their own line. Detail view lists every tag \u2014 nothing is hidden behind a +N chip.\n\nProducts can live on one chart or in a device-wide catalog (home screen \u2192 More \u2192 Products) so the same product appears in every org you map.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5j=new A.fS(B.m5,"Products and use cases",B.a1Y,null)
B.a29=new A.aR("Optional and separate from sign-in. Your Orgora account is Google Drive or OneDrive SSO \u2014 Inboxes do not create the account. From home, More \u2192 Inboxes to connect Microsoft, Gmail (app password), or Advanced (iCloud, Yahoo, IMAP) for Find people. You can connect more than one inbox.\n\nCredentials stay in the device keychain; mail is read directly from your provider. Turn scanning off at any time. Disconnecting removes that mailbox from this device; it does not sign you out of Orgora.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5k=new A.fS(B.fL,"Connect email",B.a29,null)
B.LD=new A.bK(61563,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.a2b=new A.aR("Orgora Charts maps people, reporting lines, products, and use cases. You sign in with Google Drive or Microsoft OneDrive \u2014 that cloud account is your identity. There is no separate Orgora username.\n\nAfter sign-in, Home lists your cloud charts plus the sample and LinkedIn tools. Search is in the bar. The \xb7\xb7\xb7 menu holds Backup and sync, Import from LinkedIn, Products, Inboxes, Help, and Sign out.\n\nOpen the sample chart to look around first. The sample counts toward the free-tier chart limit (three charts including the sample).",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.a5l=new A.fS(B.LD,"Getting started",B.a2b,null)
